WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.761
Scene Studio turns a recorded flight into a scene you

00:00:03.761 --> 00:00:06.516
can direct. Here are the tools to start with.

00:00:08.316 --> 00:00:12.199
Open Assets and import your own models, images, or audio.

00:00:12.199 --> 00:00:16.082
For Blender models, export a G L B file with

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.965
textures and animation included. Native blend files do not load

00:00:19.965 --> 00:00:20.353
directly.

00:00:22.153 --> 00:00:25.833
Select an object in the Scene collection. Use G, R,

00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:29.514
and S to move, rotate, and scale, or enter exact

00:00:29.514 --> 00:00:33.194
numbers. Choose World to keep it fixed, or Aircraft to

00:00:33.194 --> 00:00:34.298
follow the flight.

00:00:36.098 --> 00:00:39.630
At the playhead, save a transform key. Move to another

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:43.162
time and change the pose. The editor fills in the

00:00:43.162 --> 00:00:46.341
motion between keys. Choose smooth, linear, or hold easing.

00:00:48.141 --> 00:00:51.505
Switch to Scene mode and orbit to compose a shot.

00:00:51.505 --> 00:00:54.868
Capture a camera key, then repeat from a new view.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:58.232
The Camera tab lets you refine position, target, and field

00:00:58.232 --> 00:00:58.904
of view.

00:01:00.704 --> 00:01:05.240
In Project, adjust soundtracks, fades, lighting, and export resolution. Keep

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:09.775
the tab visible while rendering. Projects save in this browser.

00:01:09.775 --> 00:01:14.311
Use Backup to carry the recordings and assets together. Your

00:01:14.311 --> 00:01:16.125
original flight stays intact.
